WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:03.098
- Is Twitter taking a
lot from Facebook?

00:00:03.098 --> 00:00:06.031
The quickness of Twitter
is such a factor.

00:00:06.031 --> 00:00:08.133
All of you looked
at Twitter and said,

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.974
"What am I going to say?"

00:00:09.974 --> 00:00:13.042
And I said, "Holy shit. I can 
see what people are saying

00:00:13.042 --> 00:00:16.665
and engage it."
And that's why I love Twitter.

00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:19.465
People are in a false sense of
reaching mass audience

00:00:19.465 --> 00:00:22.873
in Twitter right now because of 
this enormous firehose of data.

00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:24.930
Twitter has a firehose problem.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.484
Twitter has gotten noisy.

00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:28.573
Twitter is noisy as hell.

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:31.627
Nothing is more important than
the attention of the end user.

00:00:31.627 --> 00:00:35.016
Nothing. The attention of 
the end user is the cost

00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:37.011
of entrance to
accomplish anything.

00:00:37.011 --> 00:00:39.288
Twitter's struggling. 
People don't understand it.

00:00:39.288 --> 00:00:40.869
It's losing attention.

00:00:40.869 --> 00:00:43.798
Instagram and Snapchat 
emerged as major

00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:46.053
attention grabbers 
within mobile devices.

00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:48.079
The first time I've been able
to make something trend

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:51.915
in the last three years was
this August when I sent a

00:00:51.915 --> 00:00:55.391
Snapchat to 4,000 people.

00:00:55.391 --> 00:00:58.029
And so I took a picture of myself
holding up a bottle of wine

00:00:58.029 --> 00:01:02.505
with a hashtag and after those
5,000 people in two seconds

00:01:02.505 --> 00:01:04.526
a ton of them 
posted that picture

00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:06.009
on Twitter with that hashtag

00:01:06.009 --> 00:01:07.332
and I was able to make it trend.

00:01:07.332 --> 00:01:09.646
They need to limit the things
that are being said or

00:01:09.646 --> 00:01:11.358
the amount of people.
If you don't engage with

00:01:11.358 --> 00:01:13.194
a single thing from 
a person in a year,

00:01:13.194 --> 00:01:15.635
do you need to see every
single thing they say?

00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:17.857
They're not playing 
the attention arbitrage.

00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:19.655
The amount of people who you 
follow on Twitter right now

00:01:19.655 --> 00:01:21.500
that you don't care 
about is stunning.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.846
And this is email behavior.

00:01:22.846 --> 00:01:24.781
We don't unsubscribe, we delete.

00:01:24.781 --> 00:01:27.060
But you're not going to take
the hour to unfollow.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.032
It's just the way we do things.
We don't purge.

00:01:29.032 --> 00:01:31.220
It's quicker for us to just
go through the stream.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.457
Twitter doesn't have an 
algorithm like Facebook does

00:01:34.457 --> 00:01:35.796
for the best content.

00:01:35.796 --> 00:01:38.201
- If there's this person that 
you have not clicked through

00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:40.101
on their tweet for 
a period of time,

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:41.062
six months or a year--
- Yeah.

00:01:41.062 --> 00:01:43.059
- it should be automatically
or at least prompt you

00:01:43.059 --> 00:01:44.382
do you want to delete it.

00:01:44.382 --> 00:01:46.153
- Oh you mean the way 
Facebook handles it?

00:01:46.153 --> 00:01:47.698
The biggest damn 
company in the world.

00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:49.431
I think this is the television.

00:01:49.431 --> 00:01:52.078
And that TV is the radio.
And it's 1965.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.906
I think that this is the 
number one device.

00:01:53.906 --> 00:01:57.226
And I think that YouTube,
Facebook, Instagram and

00:01:57.226 --> 00:02:00.414
Snapchat are ABC, NBC and CBS.

00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:02.455
Think of Twitter as MTV.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.273
What I think has 
happened to Twitter is that

00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:07.458
Snapchat and Instagram 
have now become ESPN,

00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:09.847
have now become the hot network.

00:02:09.847 --> 00:02:13.225
The game is changing.
Quickly and often and

00:02:13.225 --> 00:02:15.831
if you're not adjusting,
you're gonna lose.

00:02:15.831 --> 00:02:18.882
They didn't ideate the product
over a long period of time

00:02:18.882 --> 00:02:20.876
and they're paying the price.

00:02:20.876 --> 00:02:23.523
I am so intrigued by seeing
what's going to happen.

